# Title: Comma Ascent -- a ricercar on the widening third
# Composer: written for Werckmeister III; in equal temperament it has no argument
# tempo 56
# Voices: V0 soprano, V1 alto, V2 bass (tonic drone)
#
# Werckmeister III makes the major third a different size in every key. Walking
# the circle of fifths from C widens it monotonically -- 3.9, 9.7, 9.7, 15.7,
# 15.7, 15.7, 21.5 cents above a pure 5:4. Each entry states the same subject a
# fifth higher over a tonic drone, so the third is always exposed against its
# own root, and the tension rises from the TUNING while the intervals on the
# page stay identical. The collapse at bar 17 is a semitone (F#->F), from the
# widest third to the purest: 21.5 back to 3.9. Nothing about that is notated.
// Patch V0: 19
// Patch V1: 19
// Patch V2: 19

# -- C, +3.9 cents: the subject bare, over its own tonic
0     | .        | C4@72    | C3@66
2     | .        | E4@74    | -
4     | .        | D4@72    | -
5     | .        | G4@74    | -
6     | .        | F4@72    | -
7     | .        | E4@72    | -
